Cyrus closes the door and goes to his study. You head to Irene's room and knock on the door.
Irene greets you with an impatient exclamation. She is petite and flexible like a tiny snake. A green-grey cloak covers her shoulders, almost reaching the ground. Irene is fond of playing hide-and-seek and always wins.
"Henry, quickly, let's go, or we'll be late! Go-go-go!"
"Wait," you say, "Maybe we can ask your dad if he can tell us something about the island..."
"Don't! You know him, he will deliver a one-hour lecture, and we'll definitely be late!"
Cyrus is not as verbose as Nikolas Swift; maybe Irene's worries are groundless. After all, she is a fidget; it's amazing how she manages to sit still when hiding.